    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d369">

                <pb facs="0449" n="337" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg337"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/4379: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-04-29T19:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 29, 1919,
                                7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Mission requests you be informed it has been carefully considering the
                    advisability of a provisional recognition of the Kolchak Government and desires to know whether, in view of the
                    success attending the arms of the Omsk Government during the past month, you are
                    disposed to modify your views regarding such recognition as expressed in your
                    telegram to Department April 12, 4 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
